AS41E,"8th century architects John and Robert Adam were well known for their enduring and famous works in London, such as The Moffat House Hotel, Hopetoun House, Dumfries House, and most notably the neoclassical Adelphi district where Adam Street is located. This lantern was designed using common architectural elements from these timeless works of architecture. To this day, gas lanterns adorn these fabulous works.  • Handcrafted from heavy gauge solid copper for long lasting strength and beauty. • Available with electric illumination for convenient energy efficient lighting. • Solid brass hinges and latches provide superior durability and refined detailing. • Mounts and accessories built from marine grade aluminum with a corrosion resistant powder coat finish. • Compatible with standard electric bulbs including LED for customizable lighting output (bulbs not included with fixture). • Designed to withstand harsh climates with copper that naturally develops a rich, timeless patina."
